The paper’s own sharpness construction provides the decisive Track B check. For \(G_k\) with one chain edge deleted, Section 2.1 gives the coloring by a direct greedy traversal; random relabelling does not change the work, because the doubled edges expose the paired vertices and the missing edge splits the chain. I’m measuring that route against the obvious structural shortcut at the largest answer size that stays comfortably within the no-tool caps.
